Package: openmux-hardware
Version: 1.1.0
Architecture: all
Maintainer: OpenMux <support@openmux.io>
Homepage: https://github.com/OpenMux/openmux-img
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Description: OpenMux hardware identity (internal FTDI console)
 Runtime service that records the identity (manufacturer/product/serial)
 of the console's internal FTDI chip (serial EEPROM matching OMC*-A) to
 /etc/openmux-hardware, plus udev symlinks /dev/openmux/port1-8 for the
 exposed console ports. The OMC prefix is shared with 99-openmux-ftdi.rules
 here and with the factory tools' defaults in openmux-factory-tools: it is
 matched, not displayed, so all three have to move together.
